:R-HSA-190827  a            obo:GO_0008150 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Connexins follow the classical secretory transport route from the ER to the plasma membrane: ER -> ERGIC -> Golgi -> TGN (Trans Golgi Network) -> PM (Plasma Membrane). All connexins assemble or oligomerize into hexameric connexons. The site of assembly varies and depends on Cx isoform, or cell type (see Koval et al., 2006).<br>Oligomerization of connexins has been observed during ER membrane insertion (Cx32), just after exit from the ER, in the ER-Golgi-intermediate compartment (Cx26) and inside the Trans-Golgi Network (Cx43) (Falk et al. 1997; Ahmad et al. 1999; Musil and Goodenough 1993; Diez et al. 1999)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Transport of connexins along the secretory pathway" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Gilleron, J, Segretain, D, Falk, MM, 2007-01-03 12:23:09" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Edited: Matthews, L, 2007-01-26 11:57:49" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-190827" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-190861/R-HSA-190861> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

